{start_of_verse: Intro}
[C] [Am] [Dm] [G] [C]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]In the bleak [Am]midwinter, [Dm]frosty wind made [G]moan,
[C]Earth stood hard as [Am]iron, [Dm]water [G]like a [C]stone;
[Dm]Snow had fallen, [Am]snow on snow, [C]snow on [Dm]snow on [G]snow,
[C]In the bleak [Am]midwinter, [Dm]long [G][C]ago.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]Our God, Heaven cannot [Am]hold him, [Dm]nor earth [G]sustain;
[C]Heaven and earth shall [Am]flee away [Dm]when he [G]comes to [C]reign.
[Dm]In the bleak [Am]midwinter a [C]stable [Dm]place [G]sufficed
The [C]Lord God [Am]almighty, [Dm][G]Jesus [C]Christ.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]Angels and [Am]Archangels [D7]may have gathered [G]there,
[C]Cherubim and [Am]seraphim [Dm]thronged [G]the [C]air;
[Dm]But his mother [Am]only, [C]in her [Dm]maiden [G]bliss,
[C]Worshiped the [Am]beloved [Dm]with [G]a [C]kiss.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[C]What can I [Am]give him, [Dm]poor as I [G]am?
[C]If I were a [Am]shepherd, [Dm]I would [G]bring a [C]lamb;
[Dm]If I were a [Am]wise man, [C]I would [Dm]do my [G]part;
[C]Yet what I can I [Am]give him: [Dm]give [G]my [C]heart.
{end_of_verse}

